# Component platform and GPU rules

Every Darkroom installable component (CLI `launcher/components/*`, entries in `components.json`) must declare:

- `platforms`: OS list it supports (`darwin`, `win32`, `linux`), or `['*']` for all
- `gpus`: accelerator profiles it supports (`apple_silicon`, `intel_mac`, `nvidia`, `cpu`), or `['*']` for all

Never install NVIDIA-only extras by default (not in Install everything, not as silent deps):

- xformers
- SageAttention
- Triton
- TensorRT
- Nunchaku

Offer those only as optional components when an NVIDIA GPU is detected (`detectAccelProfile() === 'nvidia'` / `hasNvidiaGpu()`).

Custom nodes that need CUDA must set `requiresCuda: true` (or `gpus: ['nvidia']`) and stay optional. Doctor should warn when they are present on unsupported platforms (e.g. macOS).

GGUF support (`comfyui-gguf` / ComfyUI-GGUF) is plain PyTorch and hardware-agnostic — keep it optional, never part of Install everything, and offer it when a `.gguf` file is added or a transformer family (flux / sd3) is selected.
